  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AGD Pacific Legal Policy Twinning Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Attorney-General&apos;s Department hosted 2 senior law and justice officials from Tuvalu and Samoa as part of the Pacific Policy Champions Legal Policy Twinning Program to work on a bilateral project of significance to their country. In February 2024 an AGS lawyer prepared for and provided 1 day of pro bono training on presentation skills as part of this program. The Program is funded under the Pacific Police Development Program. This expenditure relates to AGS&apos;s delivery of training. The two projects undertaken were the drafting of a governance framework for the rollout of CCTV in Samoa and sentencing guidelines for persons convicted of sexual and gender-based violence matters in Tuvalu. The overall cost of the Program was $35,000 which was funded under the Pacific Police Development Program.</narrative>
  </description>
